# LinkedIn Anti-Bot Behavior — Evidence & Analysis

**Session**: 2026-07-29 | **Tool**: Camofox (port 9377) | **User**: fabio/hermes

## Observed Blocking Patterns

### 1. Redirect Loop on `/login`
- **Error**: "The page isn't redirecting properly. Camoufox has detected that the server is redirecting the request for this address in a way that will never complete."
- **Trigger**: Navigating to `https://www.linkedin.com/login` with valid cookies imported
- **Screenshot**: 49KB (error page with text), not blank

### 2. Blank/Black Feed Page
- **URLs**: `https://www.linkedin.com/feed/`, `https://www.linkedin.com/`, `https://www.linkedin.com/hp?original_referer=`
- **Symptoms**:
  - Screenshot: 15,103 bytes — solid dark gray/black rectangle
  - Snapshot: `totalChars: 0`, `refsCount: 0`
  - HTML via `evaluate`: `<html><head><link rel="stylesheet" href="resource://content-accessible/plaintext.css"></head><body><pre></pre></body></html>` (124 chars)
  - Tab stats: `refsCount: 0`, `toolCalls: 0-3`, `downloadsCount: 0`
- **Contrast**: `example.com` → 31KB screenshot, 237 char snapshot with refs

### 3. Cookie Import ≠ Authentication Success
- Imported 23 LinkedIn cookies (including `li_at`, `JSESSIONID`, `bcookie`, `bscookie`) for both `userId="fabio"` and `userId="hermes"`
- Cookies accepted (`ok: true, count: 23`) but session still blocked

## Root Cause Analysis

LinkedIn uses **multi-layered bot detection**:
1. **TLS/JA3 fingerprinting** — Camofox may not fully mimic Chrome TLS
2. **Canvas/WebGL fingerprinting** — Headless browsers render differently
3. **Behavioral analysis** — No mouse movements, instant navigation, no scroll
4. **Challenge pages** — Served as minimal HTML (124 chars) that doesn't render in headless
5. **Redirect traps** — `/login` loops when cookies detected but challenge fails

